AOT code caches for WoW64: guest addresses from a data area, exit linker via the thread state

Port of patches/fex/0002 (FEX 14c9268) to Madeira's FEX (3bec2ac). New
option AOTCodeCacheWIP, which only affects code cache generation; the
offline compiler turns it on. With it:
- Guest RIP constants are loaded with adrp + ldr from a data slot instead of
  a 4-instruction move that is patched on load. The immediates are resolved
  when the cache is serialized; the data area sits at a fixed distance after
  the code (aligned to 16 KiB), one slot per RELOC_GUEST_RIP_DATA_SLOT
  relocation, in relocation order.
- Jump thunks load the exit function linker from
  CpuStateFrame::Pointers.ExitFunctionLinker instead of a per-block literal.
- On the iOS host under Wine, LoadCache copies the code into its own buffer
  in the dual-mapped JIT pool with the data area after it and fills the
  slots through the RW alias.

